; (+ 1 (+ 2 (+ 3 (+ 4 5))))
;
; the longest straight-line program here, and the only one with eight steps.
;
; Run it on the artifact:   node harness/run.js wasm/milawa-verified.wasm <words>
; Run the corpus:           python3 harness/examples.py --check
;
; WORDS is the program as MVM instruction words (see wasm/milawa-verified.wat).
; EXPECT is RECORDED from the artifact by `harness/examples.py --record` and never
; written by hand; machine/examples.lisp then PROVES the model agrees with it.  So
; the file is the meeting point of a test and a proof, which is the point.
;
; Words are given with the immediates inline (CONST k, IFZ k, JMP k take the next
; word), so the listing above and the words below line up instruction by
; instruction.

words: 1 1  1 2  2  1 3  2  1 4  2  1 5  2  0
expect: halted result=15 steps=10 pc=15